This is a Franklin–Reiter related-message attack setup. 

`key` is 10 distinct lowercase ASCII letters. `rot13_key` is the ROT13 of each letter. Since ASCII lowercase is 97–122 and adding/subtracting 13 never overflows a byte (stays in [84,135]), there are **no carries**: byte-wise, each byte differs by exactly ±13.

